 "duration": 70.06,
 "text": "In the business terms, India is divided in 3 parts. India 1, 2 and 3. In the category of 1, we have 11 crores people who have more than 10 lakhs annual income. So, all of these come in our premium class. They are all tech savvy, they are influenced by western culture, they speak English etc. And they prefer convenience on the cost. Like a blanket that comes home quickly, the luggage looks a little extra. Then comes India 2. There are about 11 crores people in it. And their annual income is more than 3-4 lakhs. So, these are a little aspirational youths who want to do a lot of things. So, India 2 targets companies like Misho, Zudio, etc. Now, the interesting part is that India 3 has 120 crore people who earn less than 1.5 lakhs in a year. But now, how do these many brands earn money from them? So, basically, you don't earn money from them. Like, Facebook, YouTube, WhatsApp, these all come in India 3. So, you take their time from them. Like, on YouTube, we are taking their time from them by showing them videos. But on those videos, we have added ads on India 1's money. So, this is how it goes. Either your business is taking time from India 3, or it is taking money from India 1 and 2.",
